ollowing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SuSuSoo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SuSuSoo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SuSuSoo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SuSuSoo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SuSuSoo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SuSuSoo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SuSuSoo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-14T17:37:50Z","updated_at":"2025-12-14T17:37:50Z","body":"> Add suppor for AGENTS.md\n> \n> Refer to [agents.md](https://agents.md)\n\nI completely agree with your viewpoint. Fully implementing all features through a GUI-only approach is not the optimal solution. Over-reliance on graphical interfaces can actually reduce efficiency, especially in scenarios requiring batch processing or automation.\n\nI suggest providing AGENTS.md configuration support that's fully equivalent to the GUI functionality. Document-driven configuration offers significant advantages:\n- Easier integration with automated workflows\n- Better support for version control and configuration tracking\n- More efficient operation paths for advanced users\n- More natural and precise interaction with AI systems\n\nAt the same time, maintaining the GUI interface can still provide a friendly onboarding experience for new users. This dual-track design approach can effectively address the needs of different user groups. I hope the development team will prioritize comprehensive AGENTS.md functionality coverage to achieve parity with the GUI capabilities.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Trae-AI/TRAE/issues/comments/3651740710/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":n